    <h1>Support.</h1>

    <p><strong>Ettúi lets you save highlights and bookmarks of articles you read online.</strong></p>
    <p>Have a question, found a bug, or want to give feedback? Email us at <a href="mailto:support@ettui.com">support@ettui.com</a>. We read every message.</p>

    <h2>How to use ettúi</h2>

    <h3>Saving a highlight</h3>
    <ol>
      <li>While reading an article in <strong>Safari</strong> (or any browser that supports the iOS Share Sheet), select the text you want to remember.</li>
      <li>Tap <strong>Share</strong> → choose <strong>Ettúi</strong>.</li>
      <li>The selected text, the page URL, and the page title are saved to your account.</li>
    </ol>

    <h3>Saving a bookmark</h3>
    <p>Same as above, but <strong>don't select any text</strong> before tapping Share → Ettúi. With no selection, ettúi treats the entry as a bookmark of the whole page.</p>

    <h3>Adding tags</h3>
    <p>Right after saving from the Share Sheet, you'll see a tag chip area. Tap an existing tag to apply it, or tap the <strong>+</strong> to type a new one. Tags help you filter quotes later.</p>

    <h3>Filtering by source</h3>
    <p>In the main view, tap the <strong>filter button</strong> (bottom-right corner). Pick one or more sources. The list updates to show only items from those sources.</p>
    <p>When you filter by exactly one source, a card at the top of the view summarizes that source — tap the chevron to expand it and see all your saved items from that domain at a glance.</p>

    <h3>Searching your quotes</h3>
    <p>Pull down on the main list to reveal the search field. Searches match the highlight text.</p>

    <h3>Deleting a quote or bookmark</h3>
    <p>Long-press any card to enter selection mode. Tap as many items as you want, then tap the <strong>trash</strong> button (bottom-right) to delete them. Deletion is immediate and cannot be undone.</p>

    <h2>Accounts</h2>

    <h3>Full account vs demo account</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Demo account</strong> ("Try without an account"): no email needed; useful for trying ettúi out. Automatically deleted after <strong>48 hours of inactivity</strong>, so don't rely on it for anything important.</li>
      <li><strong>Full account</strong>: email + password. Your saved items persist until you delete them or your account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Converting a demo account to a full one</h3>
    <p>When you're signed in with a demo account, you'll see a "Demo account" banner at the top of the main view. Tap it to set an email and password and keep all your saved items.</p>

    <h3>Deleting your account</h3>
    <p>You can permanently delete your account from inside the app:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Open the filter panel (filter button → bottom-right corner).</li>
      <li><strong>Long-press your email address</strong> at the bottom of the panel.</li>
      <li>Confirm in the alert that appears.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Deletion is <strong>permanent</strong> — your account, all saved quotes, all bookmarks, all tags are removed. We can't recover them afterward.</p>

    <h3>I forgot my password</h3>
    <p>Email us at <a href="mailto:support@ettui.com">support@ettui.com</a> with the address on your account and we'll help reset it.</p>

    <h3>I can't sign in</h3>
    <p>Most often this is a wrong email/password combo or a network issue. Try again with the same details, then close and reopen the app. If it still fails, email us with a screenshot of the error and the iOS version you're on.</p>

    <h2>Found a bug?</h2>
    <p>We'd like to know. Email <a href="mailto:support@ettui.com">support@ettui.com</a> with:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>A short description of what happened.</li>
      <li>A screenshot or screen recording, if possible.</li>
      <li>Your iOS version (Settings → General → About → iOS Version).</li>
      <li>Your ettúi app version (you'll find this on the App Store page or in the iOS Settings app).</li>
    </ul>

